97869484,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4josOs","name":"resterm_Linux_x86_64.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":87,"digest":"sha256:9995950f0d9413dc9b08a2ecaa7d7e98d2d3ddbcce99a869e797ff8b1d14df1b","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:40Z"},{"id":597869489,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4josOx","name":"resterm_Windows_arm64.exe","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":64483840,"digest":"sha256:97f4e7aa4c20d28f99b3e45c57143a254fa695568d8fa60cb0240ca2d8b90cd0","download_count":9,"created_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:43Z"},{"id":597869486,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4josOu","name":"resterm_Windows_arm64.exe.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":92,"digest":"sha256:32085232ff7b681702a8348376520780c5328c0033520e067b2a97f42ccf1ca6","download_count":19,"created_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:40Z"},{"id":597869503,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4josO_","name":"resterm_Windows_x86_64.exe","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":69281280,"digest":"sha256:e7a7be9536f127f799ec9f4914942c2a5866b7447759f854d6e1a9bac57d351f","download_count":44,"created_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:43Z"},{"id":597869498,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4josO6","name":"resterm_Windows_x86_64.exe.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":93,"digest":"sha256:2c2280fb4f8fd6fe2d29772c67201c0814d41fe1971c852b4a28c0900e5f5742","download_count":19,"created_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T09:57:40Z"}],"body":"## v1.10.2\r\n\r\nResterm now picks the file type itself and opens only reconized types.\r\n\r\n## If you are on 1.9.x\r\n\r\n- [1.10.0](https://github.com/unkn0wn-root/resterm/releases/tag/v1.10.0) adds `cmd=` for command auth and named command auth with `use=`. Options with spaces around `=` and unknown `@auth command` options are now errors. The Headers tab has a one-line summary and shows each repeated header on its own line.\r\n- [1.10.1](https://github.com/unkn0wn-root/resterm/releases/tag/v1.10.1) names a command auth definition with `name=`, as in `# @auth global command name=gh cmd=\"gh auth token\"`. A plain word after `command` is now an error, because in 1.10.0 it could turn off auth without an error.\r\n\r\n## Open in external app\r\n\r\nIn previous versions, the extension came from the file name the server sent or the URL. A body sent with `filename=\"setup.exe\"` was written as `resterm-2849.exe` and handed to the default app. On Windows, this could e.g., run a program sent by the server. HTML and SVG bodies opened in the browser, where their scripts could run.\r\n\r\nNow the extension always comes from the type. This body opens as `invoice.pdf`:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nContent-Type: application/pdf\r\nContent-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"invoice.exe\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n- Resterm finds the type from the `Content-Type` header, then the file name the server sent, then the body itself.\r\n- Only these types open: images, PDF, plain text, JSON, YAML, CSV, audio, video, zip and gzip archives, and Office files without macros (`.docx`, `.xlsx`, `.pptx`).\r\n- HTML, SVG, XML, and Markdown open as `.txt`, so scripts inside them cannot run.\r\n- When a type is not known, nothing opens and the status bar shows `Can't pick a safe app for this body. Save it with g Shift+S.`\r\n\r\nOpened files:\r\n\r\n- Files keep the server's name, so the TUI shows `invoice.pdf` instead of `resterm-2849.pdf`.\r\n- Files go to a private temp folder that Resterm deletes when it exits. In 1.10.1, they stayed in the system temp folder.\r\n- Resterm waits for the opener, so it no longer leaves any processes behind. If the opener fails right away, the status bar shows the error and points to `g Shift+S` (save to file).\r\n- The response command bar shows `Open` next to `Save` on the Pretty and Raw tabs.\r\n\r\n## Save names\r\n\r\nThe name suggested by `g Shift+S` also changed:\r\n\r\n- Common types get their usual extension. `audio/mpeg` saves as `.mp3`, and `+json` and `+xml` types such as `application/problem+json` save as `.json` and `.xml`.\r\n- A name that Windows treats as a device, such as `CON`, `AUX`, `NUL`, or `COM1`, gets a `_` prefix. `CON.pdf` saves as `_CON.pdf`. Opened files get the same prefix.\r\n\r\n## Changed\r\n\r\n- `g Shift+E` no longer opens executables, e.g., Office files that can hold macros (`.doc`, `.xls`, `.ppt`), or bodies with no known type. Save them with `g Shift+S` and open yourself.\r\n"}
